      "message": "I think the current mock is fine but I\u0027m still not quite satisfied with the need to always define both the inputs and outputs in tests.\n\nIdeally, you would have a default mock that returns default values for all commands which is initially in a disconnected state. Any changes we want to test should then be introduced in the test itself.\n\nFor example, an initialization test would look like the following:\n\n```\nTEST_F(OpmUnitTest, Initialize) {\n  // Always start with PPM reset.\n  EXPECT_CALL(pd_mock_, MatchCmd(UCSI_CMD_PPM_RESET)).Times(Exactly(1));\n  EXPECT_CALL(pd_mock_, MatchCmdList({UCSI_CMD_SET_NOTIFICATION, UCSI_CMD_GET_CAPABILITY, UCSI_CMD_GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS, UCSI_CMD_GET_PDOS, UCSI_CMD_GET_ALTERNATE_MODES}).Times(AtLeast(1));\n  \n  StartMainloop();\n}\n```\n\nThen I\u0027d want to test that alternate modes are properly populated:\n\n```\nTEST_F(OpmUnitTest, Init_PortAltModesPopulated) {\n  SyfsVerifier verifier;\n\n  EXPECT_CALL(pd_mock_, MatchCmd(UCSI_GET_CAPABILITY)).WillRepeatedly(Invoke(kGetCapWithBasicAltmodes, fptr));\n  EXPECT_CALL(pd_mock_, MatchGetAltMode(kSop, _)).WillRepeatedly(Invoke(kGetAltModeForSop, fptr));\n  \n  StartMainLoop();\n  \n  verifier.VerifyPortAltModes();\n}\n```\n\nI think the current set of tests may provide this already but do too much in a single test. Let\u0027s commit this for now and refactor the tests to split up functionality more.",
      "revId": "91c707a768c2ee476275de15d5a483fa5f289e2b",
